## What changed

- replace the three-seed `1.96 × SE` half-width with the correct two-sided Student-t interval for `df = 2`;
- report one-seed Smoke uncertainty as not estimable instead of zero;
- record checkpoint SHA-256 and byte size in every evaluation configuration;
- verify the exact route-by-seed checkpoint paths and their links to all evaluation states before packaging;
- verify ZIP CRC, the artifact file manifest, and checkpoint counts in both Kaggle notebooks;
- update the release version and protocol documentation to `v0.1.5-confirmatory`.

## Why

The Full Kaggle artifact preserved valid raw confusion counts and route means, but its summary script used the normal critical value while labeling the result as a 95% run-level interval. With only three model seeds, this understated uncertainty. The returned archive also excluded checkpoint weights without retaining a verifiable link between each evaluation and the exact validation-selected checkpoint.

## Impact

No GPU rerun is required to correct the existing manuscript statistics because the raw per-evaluation results are complete. Future runs will produce correct intervals and stronger checkpoint-to-evaluation provenance automatically.

## Validation

- repository audit: 32 checks passed;
- Ruff lint and formatting checks passed;
- Python compilation and shell syntax passed;
- Full artifact interval recomputation matched the independent df=2 result;
- synthetic packaging regression verified five expected checkpoint hashes and their evaluation links.

## Root cause

`load_split_manifest(...)` accepted the same logical sequence reference in multiple splits. The split filter normalizes path-like references, so entries such as `seq001` and `./seq001/` both select the same sequence even when placed in `train` and `val` respectively.

This silently permits train/validation or train/test leakage and can make evaluation results invalid while the manifest still appears structurally correct.

## Fix

- validate every loaded manifest at the public split-manifest boundary;
- normalize sequence references with the same path normalization used by split filtering;
- reject references owned by more than one split with a deterministic, split-specific error;
- retain distinct full paths such as `site_a/seq001` and `site_b/seq001`.

## Tests

Added focused regressions for:

- an exact duplicate sequence assigned to `train` and `val`;
- path-equivalent references (`seq001` versus `./seq001/`);
- distinct paths sharing only the same basename.

## Validation

- Python bytecode compilation passed for the modified guard;
- a dependency-light semantic harness reproduced the pre-fix overlap and verified fail-closed behavior;
- changed Python lines satisfy the repository's 100-character limit;
- branch comparison: 2 commits ahead, 0 behind current `main`, changing one guard and one focused test module.

GitHub Actions provides the authoritative repository-wide pytest and Ruff validation.
